window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>HE PLANNED TO OBLITERATE AN ENTIRE CITY. HE THOUGHT NO ONE COULD STAND IN HIS WAY. BUT HE HADN'T HEARD OF RIYRIA.</p> <p>When a master-craftsmen dwarf is fired, he threatens retaliation. The rogues-for-hire known as Riyria are commissioned to find and stop him. Traveling to the paradise resort of Tur Del Fur, the two are granted a lavish allowance that, along with the easy job, promises to turn the trip into a vacation.</p> <p>Everything would have been perfect except that the disgruntled employee’s last name is Berling and the target of his wrath is the legendary towers of Drumindor.</p> <p>It's been more than five years since the last adventure with Royce Melborn (a cynical ex-assassin) and Hadrian Blackwater (an idealistic ex-mercenary), a pair whose bonds of friendship are bound with blood. This is the 20th novel based in the world of Elan and the fifth in the Riyria Chronicle series.</p> <p>Adapted from the novel and produced with a full cast of actors, immersive sound effects and cinematic music!</p> <p>Narrated by Bradley Foster Smith. Featuring Danny Gavigan as Royce, Chris Genebach as Hadrian, Terence Aselford as Albert and Arcadius, Nora Achrati as Gwen, Andrew James Spooner as Auberon, Bradley Foster Smith as Gravis, Jenna Sharpe as Constance and Opal, and Zura Johnson as Sloan. With additional performances by Peter Holdway, Emlyn McFarland, Stewart Crank, Chris Davenport, Christopher Tester, Nathaniel Priestley, Kay Elúvian, Joe Mallon, Matthew McGee, RJ Bayley, Rose Elizabeth Supan, James Lewis, Matthew Bassett, Michael John Casey, Nanette Savard, Robb Moreira, David Arden Engel, Wyn Delano, Danielle Cohen, Donald Guzzi, Kymberley Cochrane, Christopher Walker, Jonathan David Bullock, Hedra Knight, Damon Alums, Dawn Ursula, Steve Wannall, Holly Adams, Eric Messner, Drew Kopas, Richard Rohan, Kymberley Cochrane, Mort Shelby, and Jessica Schly.</p>"; 
